Survival exists to resist unnecessary loss.

The Continuity Problem

Every generation faces a recurring challenge:

Create
↓
Lose
↓
Rediscover
↓
Repeat

The ecosystem seeks to reduce unnecessary rediscovery through continuity.

Knowledge should not need to be rebuilt from zero every generation.

What Should Survive

Not everything deserves preservation.

Survival efforts should prioritize:

Principles

Foundational truths and guiding ideas.

Methods

Repeatable mechanisms that generate understanding.

Standards

Practices that improve reliability and continuity.

Knowledge

Validated understanding.

Heritage

Lessons and contributions considered valuable across generations.

Identity

The continuity of purpose and direction.

